  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "For the 2026 tax season (2025 tax year), you can get an automatic, free extension to file your federal return until October 15, 2026, by submitting Form 4868 by April 15, 2026. An extension provides extra time to file, not to pay. Taxes owed are still due by April 15 to avoid penalties.Key Tax Extension Information for 2026Extension Deadline: April 15, 2026 (must be filed by this date).New Return Deadline: October 15, 2026.How to File: Use IRS Free File or tax software to submit Form 4868, or pay via Direct Pay and select \"Extension\" as the reason.Special Considerations: If you live in a disaster area (e.g., specific Mississippi areas until June 8, or Tennessee areas), you may have an automatic extension without filing Form 4868.Penalties and PaymentFailure to File Penalty: This is significantly higher than the failure-to-pay penalty. Filing an extension avoids this.If You Owe: Estimate your total tax liability and pay what you can by April 15 to minimize interest and penalties.Payment Options: You can pay online, by phone, or mobile device using IRS services like Direct Pay, or use software to pay via credit/debit card.State Tax ExtensionsMost states accept the federal extension automatically or require a separate form, usually available when you file a state return with software.Further Exploration:Read the Guide to filing your taxes in 2026 from the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau for a comprehensive overview of the process.TurboTax offers a dedicated page to help you file your extension and provides, in a guide, tips on navigating the process.If you cannot pay your full tax bill by the deadline, pay as much as you can and file an extension to minimize penalties, then explore IRS payment plans.",
